\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Reversing a Fourier mode}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Let #{z} be the multiplier of a [shift](fdip-00AN) on a Fourier
mode around one circle. A step in the opposite direction multiplies
the same mode by #{z^{-1}}. If two circles have the same period,
their coordinates can also exchange places. Then the two corresponding
multipliers exchange places. Which combinations of reversals and
exchanges return every multiplier to its original coordinate?}
